E["subzone:sunnyglade"] = {t="subzone",n="Sunnyglade",z="riverglades",s="Sunnyglade was once a wealthy, prosperous human settlement belonging to the kingdom of Stormwind during the First War. Devastated and eventually abandoned as the front lines collapsed, the ruined settlement now languishes under the dark influence of the Twilight's Hammer cult.",h="Sunnyglade was once a wealthy, prosperous human settlement belonging to the kingdom of Stormwind during the...",sec={{t="Fall of a Golden Town",b="Before the First War tore southern Azeroth apart, Sunnyglade was celebrated for its wealth and comfortable prosperity. That peace was violently shattered when the Old Horde invaded. Orc raiding parties attacked the town and enslaved its surviving residents, leaving only a lone wizard's tower intact to study the arcane arts of human conjurers. Though Stormwind forces mounted an effort to rescue the captive peasants and rebuild the settlement, the surrounding Riverglades were steadily swallowed by the advancing Horde. Deeming the outer province lost, Stormwind's commanders eventually withdrew their resources to defend the homeland, leaving Sunnyglade to ruin.",sp=0},{t="A Blighted Refuge",b="Today, Sunnyglade lies far beyond the safe borders of Stormwind's reestablished realm. While the iconic stone mage tower remarkably weathered the First War and the years of abandonment that followed, the peaceful township around it is gone. Instead, the secluded ruins have been occupied by zealots of the Twilight's Hammer cult, who turn the once-prosperous valley to their own sinister designs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to Sunnyglade?",a="Sunnyglade was attacked and sacked by the Old Horde during the First War. Although human forces managed to liberate captive peasants and attempted to rebuild, Stormwind ultimately abandoned the Riverglades region to focus on defending its core territories.",al={"what is sunnyglade","sunnyglade history","why is sunnyglade destroyed"}},{q="Who controls Sunnyglade now?",a="The ruins of Sunnyglade are currently occupied by the Twilight's Hammer cult, who have set up camp amidst the broken houses and ancient wizard's tower.",al={"who lives in sunnyglade","sunnyglade enemies","sunnyglade twilight"}},{q="Why did the orcs leave the mage tower standing during the First War?",a="When the Old Horde sacked Sunnyglade, they deliberately spared the town's arcane tower so their warlocks and commanders could study human magic and unravel its secrets.",al={"orc mage tower sunnyglade","sunnyglade tower lore"}},{q="Why didn't Stormwind reclaim the town after the war?",a="As the First War intensified, Stormwind leadership judged the Riverglades to be lost territory and redirected all military focus toward the kingdom's central defense, leaving Sunnyglade behind.",al={"why abandoned","stormwind sunnyglade"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The solitary wizard's tower of Sunnyglade is an eerie reminder of early human spellcraft, once spared by the Old Horde solely so they could dissect human arcane knowledge.",["race:Human"]="The overgrown stones of Sunnyglade serve as a somber monument to the outer settlements abandoned when Stormwind was forced to pull back during the First War."},kw={"first war","mage tower","old horde","riverglades","stormwind","sunnyglade","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:riverglades","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:first-war","topic:old-horde","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:redridge"},src={"Sunnyglade"}}
E["zone:riverglades"] = {t="zone",n="Riverglades",z="riverglades",s="The Riverglades is a contested river valley east of the Burning Steppes and Badlands, historically claimed by the Kingdom of Stormwind. Overrun by the Old Horde during the First War and largely abandoned by the crown, the region remains a battleground as local human loyalists clash with modern Horde outposts and local wildlife. It borders Redridge Mountains to the southwest, Swamp of Sorrows to the south, and faces Tanaris across the sea.",h="The Riverglades is a contested river valley east of the Burning Steppes and Badlands, historically claimed by...",sec={{t="A Forgotten Borderland",b="Historically part of the Kingdom of Stormwind, the Riverglades fell into ruin during the First War when the Old Horde swept through the region. Its central settlement, Sunnyglade, was sacked by the orcs, who spared its mage tower solely to study human sorcery before enslaving the surviving townsfolk. Though Stormwind soldiers mounted an effort to liberate the captives and rebuild, the kingdom eventually deemed the entire valley lost and diverted resources toward defending the core homelands. For years, the region remained largely cut off from formal crown support.",sp=0},{t="The Struggle for Farholde",b="Despite being left behind by Stormwind's higher leadership, the human defenders never fully surrendered their homeland. Under Knight Commander Demar Brant of the legendary Brotherhood of the Horse, the remaining loyalists hold Farholde Keep as a bastion against the wilderness and hostile invaders. Meanwhile, the modern Horde maintains their own strong presence nearby at outposts like Rog'mar and Bolder'ok, ensuring that the ancient conflict over the glades continues to smolder.",sp=0},{t="Geography and Travel",b="Stretching along the coast of the Forbidding Sea, the Riverglades is flanked by mountainous terrain and winding waterways. Travelers on foot can cross west through Blackrock Pass to the Burning Steppes, wind southwest through Redridge Pass toward the Redridge Mountains, navigate south into the Swamp of Sorrows, or trek northwest past Twilight's Shroud into the Badlands. On the coast, Powderfuse Port provides sea passage connecting directly across the ocean to Steamwheedle Port in Tanaris.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Riverglades?",a="The Riverglades is a contested region lying east of the Badlands and Burning Steppes, fronting the Forbidding Sea. Once a flourishing territory of Stormwind, it is now an active frontier contested by the Alliance at Farholde Keep and the Horde at Rog'mar.",al={"riverglades overview","what is this zone","about riverglades"}},{q="What happened to Sunnyglade?",a="Sunnyglade was raided and destroyed by the Old Horde during the First War. The orcs captured the surviving villagers as slaves and kept a local mage tower intact to decipher human magic. Although Stormwind soldiers freed the captives and tried to rebuild, the kingdom ultimately abandoned the area to focus on its western borders.",al={"sunnyglade history","fall of sunnyglade","what happened to the town"}},{q="Who controls Farholde Keep?",a="Farholde Keep is held by Alliance loyalists led by Knight Commander Demar Brant of the Brotherhood of the Horse. His forces have spent years fighting to reclaim the Riverglades after Stormwind originally wrote the territory off as lost.",al={"who leads farholde","alliance in riverglades","brotherhood of the horse"}},{q="How do you reach Tanaris from the Riverglades?",a="A coastal boat runs regularly between Powderfuse Port on the eastern shore of the Riverglades and Steamwheedle Port in Tanaris, offering a direct naval link across the sea.",al={"boat to tanaris","powderfuse port boat","how to get to tanaris"}},{q="What passes lead into other zones?",a="You can travel southwest through Redridge Pass to reach the Redridge Mountains, or cross south directly toward the Swamp of Sorrows. To the west, Blackrock Pass leads past the Bristle Hills to the Burning Steppes, while the trails north of Twilight's Shroud run directly into the Badlands.",al={"how to get to redridge","passes from riverglades","exits from riverglades"}},{q="What is Krol'dok Stronghold?",a="Krol'dok Stronghold is a fortified dungeon complex in the Riverglades, representing a major seat of hostile power in the contested territory.",al={"kroldok stronghold","riverglades dungeon","what dungeon is here"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance soldiers find old wounds laid bare in the Riverglades, where remnants of the Brotherhood of the Horse continue an unsung crusade to take back land Stormwind abandoned during the First War.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, establishing outposts like Rog'mar ensures a secure coastal foothold and keeps pressure on old human strongholds lingering east of Redridge.",["race:Human"]="Human travelers witness a tragic chapter of their own heritage in Sunnyglade, a reminder of the First War's heavy toll on the eastern frontier of their kingdom."},kw={"blackrock pass","brotherhood of the horse","demar brant","farholde keep","krol'dok stronghold","powderfuse port","redridge pass","riverglades","rog'mar","sunnyglade"},rel={"subzone:sunnyglade","subzone:blackrock-pass","zone:redridge","zone:badlands","zone:swampofsorrows","zone:burningsteppes","subzone:steamwheedle-port"},src={"Riverglades"}}
